{
  "_comment": [
    "The ONLY place kie.ai knowledge lives. Skill prose must never carry a model id,",
    "endpoint or price -- see cli/README.md.",
    "",
    "`verified` is false until a real job has succeeded on that model. `kie video` warns",
    "loudly on an unverified model and `kie doctor` reports the count. Flip it by hand",
    "(or let `kie video` flip it on first success) once you've seen output.",
    "",
    "Prices are USD per generation and are ESTIMATES used for budget refusal. kie.ai",
    "exposes no cost-estimate endpoint -- only an account credit balance -- so every",
    "number here was entered by hand and must be reconciled against `kie spend`.",
    "`input` carries the model's REAL request contract, captured from its own doc page: required fields, defaults, types (wan wants duration as a string, seedance as an integer -- this bites) and the per-model names for reference inputs. schemaVerified:false means the contract here is still a guess and the CLI says so before spending.",
    "measuredCredits is a FACT from a real job (see runs/.ledger.jsonl); priceUsd remains an estimate. A 4s 480p video cost 46.8 credits against a 7-credit image -- video is ~7x an image here, so budget in credits, not in the USD guesses."
  ],
  "captured": "2026-09-10",
  "staleAfterDays": 30,
